{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1540470095,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzAyOTA5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2948#issuecomment-433029090"},"message":"\u003e Such branch would get a different dataset id than 'master' one way or another (including even no id at all unless create is also called on that branch). I think that's fine, since the orphan branch actually has no common history with master. \n\nI think that's fine too.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540480049,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzA4ODQzOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2948#issuecomment-433088438"},"message":"@kyleam : If it is to stay that way, I'd need to adapt that `rerun` test I mentioned above. It states, that it does checkout out that orphan branch to test the \"one commit in a repo\" case. Now, there'd be two options:\n1. Call `create` before in order to have a dataset id. That seems to make the test case pointless, since there'd be a commit before the run record.\n2. `run` would need to be able to record `None` as the dataset id. But what would be the correct behavior of `rerun` in that case?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540480235,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzA4OTU4Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2948#issuecomment-433089587"},"message":"I think `None` would be ok and as long as `rerun` only compares (None == None) everything is fine. But I wonder whether this would have unwanted implications later on, when there is a dataset id.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540480235,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE0NDUwMjUzMA=="},"target":"2be89185633396130834d9ddaae0de157d9676d7352c56353c32d1983427acdb","message":"I think `None` would be ok as long as `rerun` only compares (None == None) everything is fine. But I wonder whether this would have unwanted implications later on, when there is a dataset id.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1540481196,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzA5NTU5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2948#issuecomment-433095591"},"message":"\u003e Now, there'd be two options:\n\nYes, it'd need to be number one.\n\n\u003e I think None would be ok as long as rerun only compares (None == None) everything is fine. But I wonder whether this would have unwanted implications later on, when there is a dataset id.\n\nIf a later commit adds the dataset ID, a rerun won't compare `None` to `None`.  It will just run it:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/f9355351d1eee7747ee226f357f9c9c2d045a6f5/datalad/interface/rerun.py#L333-L340","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1540481196,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE0NDUxMDE2NA=="},"target":"208f6654a808d45cbe3baccaa7433df88ec082fbb40bf6420a4cf5954ce6ab9b","message":"\u003e Now, there'd be two options:\n\nYes, it'd need to be number ~one~ two (edit: doh).\n\n\u003e I think None would be ok as long as rerun only compares (None == None) everything is fine. But I wonder whether this would have unwanted implications later on, when there is a dataset id.\n\nIf a later commit adds the dataset ID, a rerun won't compare `None` to `None`.  It will just run it:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/f9355351d1eee7747ee226f357f9c9c2d045a6f5/datalad/interface/rerun.py#L333-L340","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1540481558,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzA5ODEyOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2948#issuecomment-433098129"},"message":"\u003e If a later commit adds the dataset ID, a rerun won't compare None to None. It will just run it:\n\nSo I think the above check should just be updated to also \"just run\" when `dset.id is None`, probably logging a warning as well.  There shouldn't be a need to store `None`.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1540481558,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE0NDUxMzA4MQ=="},"target":"6a7c57b5af0e8607aa45c99bfac25ad4545eaf8dd0024c5e90403da00b1cb594","message":"\u003e If a later commit adds the dataset ID, a rerun won't compare None to None. It will just run it:\n\nSo I think the above check should just be updated to also \"just run\" when `dset.id is None`, probably logging a warning as well.  There shouldn't be a need to store `None` in the run record.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540481818,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzA5OTk2MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2948#issuecomment-433099961"},"message":"Yes, I think I just need to fix `GitRepo.checkout` to reload `config` and be done. This should result in the correct dataset id (None) when `run` is called and that's it. The test should then still run on an empty branch with no need to further changes. Thanks!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1540482877,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzEwNjU5Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2948#issuecomment-433106597"},"message":"\u003e Yes, I think I just need to fix GitRepo.checkout to reload config and be done\n\nMakes sense.  Thanks.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540485243,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzEyMDI3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2948#issuecomment-433120272"},"message":"\u003e Makes sense. Thanks.\n\nFTR:\nBut sadly it's insufficient. This is because it's not necessarily the checkout that might change `.datalad/config`, but `git reset` (as is case with this test). For now I'll do the additional reload just within the test and make the question on when to reload config in that context a separate issue.","files":null}]}